ployee experiences are built, measured and scaled.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Onboarding Experience:</strong> You help us design and deliver a seamless start for new hires, ensuring they have the perfect first day and a structured integration over their first weeks and months with the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Event Architect</strong>: You support the concept and planning of our internal "Flip Events" (e.g., Team &amp; Culture Days). Your presence in the Stuttgart office (at least once a week) is key to bringing these events to life and engaging with the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Process Automation &amp; Optimization:</strong> With a fresh perspective, you create smart workflows, automate manual tasks, and ensure maximum efficiency in our daily operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>HR Analytics:</strong> You manage our data quality and transform raw information into insightful HR reports and dashboards to drive data-based decision-making.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you bring to the table</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re currently studying Business Administration, Psychology, Economics, Business Psychology, or a related field and ideally have 5–6 months available for an internship.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First experience in HR, Recruiting, or Active Sourcing is a plus - but not a must.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Passion for creative ideas and innovative approaches to talent sourcing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident in using social networks and comfortable with digital tools and AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and empathy to create a positive Employee &amp; Candidate Journey.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills, initiative