plex and high-velocity sales cycles from discovery and solution design through sophisticated contract negotiations and high-touch implementation handovers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Consistently outperform monthly MRR targets by applying an entrepreneurial mindset to territory management, focusing on high-LTV (Long Term Value) accounts and portfolio expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide clients from needs analysis and solution design through proposals, contract agreements, and seamless onboarding.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver high-impact presentations and live demonstrations that translate Lightspeed’s technical capabilities into clear business outcomes for owners and operators.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain a rigorous, high-integrity Salesforce pipeline; managing your own workload and updating the team accordingly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spearhead outbound initiatives and represent the brand at premier industry events to cultivate a high-quality pipeline and build long-term leads.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you need to bring:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years of high-performance experience in Field or Outbound sales, with a track record of navigating complex, solution-based sales within the technology, SaaS, or hospitality ecosystems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A deep understanding of the hospitality industry, including key segments and operational considerations is ideal</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced in sales development best practice - building pipelines, territory planning, and driving new business with strong organisational ability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated success in consistently exceeding aggressive MRR targets and significantly contributing to regional market-share expansion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficient in using Salesforce or similar CRM systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A self-starting, agile mindset with the ability to operate autonomously in a high-growth, fast-paced environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What's in it for you?</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Come live the Lightspeed Experience…</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine career growth opportunities based on performance within a company that's continuously expanding</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with highly skilled people who are as passionate about sales &amp; marketing  as you are</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An environment that encourages initiatives and leadership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work in a team big enough for growth but lean enough to make a real impact</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fun activities with your teammates &amp; social events throughout the year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Opportunity to learn, expand your skill set, forge wonderful relationships and make your mark within the diverse and inclusive Lightspeed culture, a true Canadian tech success story</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">… and enjoy a range of benefits that’ll keep you happy and healthy:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed equity scheme (we are all owners)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible Paid Time Off - providing you the freedom to take time off however you like</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private Medical Insurance and cash health plan for optical, dental and more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Health &amp; Wellness Credit- expense up to 400 GBP per year towards your gym membership, yoga classes, a new bike or whatever else you do for your health </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental Health Support through the LifeWorks and Modern Health Apps- whether it is meditation, coaching or counseling you need - each employee gets access to this platform </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time off to volunteer and give back to your community</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transit / parking benefit - for when you need to travel to the Belfast office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A variety of drinks &amp; snacks in our offices in London </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>To all recruitment agencies: Lightspeed does not accept unsolicited agency resumes. If we have not directly engaged your company in writing to supply candidates for a specific vacancy, Lightspeed will not be responsible for any fees related to unsolicited resumes.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Lightspeed is a proud equal opportunity employer and we are committed to creating an inclusive and barrier-free workplace. Lightspeed welcomes and encourages applications from people with disabilities. Accommodations are available on request for candidates taking part in all aspects of the selection process.</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Where to from here?</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Obviously, this has to be mutually beneficial: we want you to step into a role you love, and we want to offer you a place you’re proud to come to every day. For a glimpse into our world check out our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/careers/">career page here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed is building communities through commerce, and we need people from all backgrounds and lived experiences to do that. We were founded in 2005, in Montreal’s gay village and our original members were all part of the LGBTQ+ community. The ethos of our business has been about inclusion from the very beginning, and we strive to provide a workplace where everyone belongs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who we are:</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Powering the businesses that are the backbone of the global economy, Lightspeed's one-stop commerce platform helps merchants innovate to simplify, scale, and provide exceptional customer experiences. Our cloud commerce solution transforms and unifies online and physical operations, multichannel sales, expansion to new locations, global payments, financial solutions, and connection to supplier networks.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Montréal, Canada in 2005, Lightspeed is dual-listed on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: LSPD) and Toronto Stock Exchange (TSX: LSPD). With teams across North America, Europe, and Asia Pacific, the company serves retail, hospitality, and golf businesses in over 100 countries.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lightspeed handles your information in accordance with our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="c-link" href="https://www.lightspeedhq.com/legal/applicant-privacy-statement/">Applicant Privacy Statement</a>.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/lightspeedhq/senior-field-account-executive-belfast-404036","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Belfast","created_at":1792431619},{"slug":"account-executive-london-29480","company_name":"Light Inc","title":"Account Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Retire the ERP.<br /></strong><br />Light exists to replace factory-era ERPs with software that feels alive. Our Smart Financial Platform gives modern, global companies superpowers—automated accounting, real-time reporting, and financial flows that move at the speed of the business.<br /><br />We build with our customers, ship fast, and obsess over craft. In a short time, Light has gone from idea to the operating core for leading companies like Lovable, Legora, and Keyshot. People don’t just use Light—they enjoy it.<br /><br />We’re an early team defining a new software category. Think engineers who love debits and credits, designers who care about reconciliation states, and operators who treat finance as a product. If you’re excited to modernize how the world runs money—one workflow at a time—you’re in the right place.<br /><br />Backed by world-class investors and advised by industry titans, we’re building category-defining products with the freedom to ship ambitiously and own outcomes.<br />Come help us make Light the global default for next-gen finance.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Account Executive role:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leading sales cycles for Light as an SFP, managing deals from $30K to $200K+ and consistently hitting revenue targets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Building relationships with C-suite executives and key decision makers, understanding their business needs and showing how our SFP solution helps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creating account plans and working closely with technical teams to develop solutions for target industries like asset-light, multinational companies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Running effective customer meetings and negotiations, handling complex deals from first contact through contract signing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Owning the AE to BDR relationship to generate pipeline as a team.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />How you fit into the team:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your main mission is to help prospective customers see the light. Aside from being based in-office in London or New York, this role requires you to be hungry, have an understanding of finance tools and knowledge of sales. We have a clear ICP defined with a leadlist.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a GTM role with the responsibility of sales and closing pipeline. You'll work with a small and stellar team with a deep understanding of the market who has done this before.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />Your qualifications:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3-6 years of closing experience and acing pipeline - preferably within ERPs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Your Personality</em>: Your exceptional interpersonal skills, energy and sense of ownership make you stand out.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Thriving in a Fast-Paced Environment: </em>You thrive in a fast-paced, high-growth, and rapidly changing environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Attention to Detail: </em>Your attention to detail, outstanding communication skills (phone, listening, and writing), set you up for success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Self-Driven:</em> Self-driven and ambitious, you have the desire to grow with Light.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Entrepreneurial Spirit: </em>Your entrepreneurial spirit and experience with a strong growth mindset align perfectly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Comfort in Quota-Carrying Environment:</em> You are ambitious, self-motivated, and comfortable working in a quota-carrying environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical experience using AI or emerging technology tools to improve productivity, insight, or decision-making, with the ability to apply first-principles thinking to new problems.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />Bonus points:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're CPA and have a few years of experience within Big4, accounting or the CFO suite.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sales Tools Familiarity: You have prior experience using Sales Automation/Prospecting Tools (e.g., Amplemarket, Salesloft, Outreach) and CRM (Hubspot).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Startup Experience: You've worked at a fast-growing startup.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cold Calling Pro: You ace cold calling and relationship building. Wanna really get on our radar? Find our number, call and pitch us.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />A few tips to stand out</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Show us who you are through your application and don't limit yourself to a resume. Try not to be generic.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have numbers to show so you can measure impact? Even better!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Most people can say they wanna work in a startup, but why this one? What are your expectations and what do you specifically wanna learn from us?</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />The good stuff</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In addition to being part of a great team and working in a really fun and innovative environment, we offer:<br />💸 A competitive salary + potential stock options<br />🏝 25 days of annual leave + public holidays in the country where you are based.<br />🥳 Regular socials and company off-sites<br />🚀 A huge opportunity for career growth as you'll help shape a market-defining product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong><br />The famous last words</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working at Light means you're embarking on an exciting journey to reshape the future of multinational financial operations. Our cheat-code is that we've built something like this before - and are now doing it again, only better. Our goal is to make global finance effortless and empower companies to make informed decisions.<br /><br />🚀 Join the rocket ship while it's taking off 🚀</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/light-inc/account-executive-london-29480","tags":["GTM"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792431617},{"slug":"staff-software-engineer-data-enrichment-platform-london-united-kingdom-26859","company_name":"Wayve","title":"Staff Software Engineer, Data Enrichment Platform","description":"<div><div style="left:0px;width:100%;height:0px;position:relative;padding-bottom:56.25%"><iframe src="https://embedded-media.ashbyhq.com/embed/c3dedbb7-82c2-4668-a1bf-b53c8f870af0/8c1bb54c-6e60-48b5-8dbb-5631ddd06204" style="top:0px;left:0px;width:100%;height:100%;position:absolute;border:0px" allowfullscreen="true" scrolling="no" allow="encrypted-media *; picture-in-picture *;" sandbox="allow-scripts allow-same-origin allow-presentation"></iframe></div></div><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Before the detail, here's the challenge you'd help us solve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We build the embodied intelligence that moves real vehicles safely, and the ecosystem a billion machines will run on in the future. Very few people in AI can say this. Every role here, whatever the team, plugs into that.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Here’s what this particular role covers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🛠️ About our Data Enrichment Platform Team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our Enrichment Orchestration team builds the platform that enables Wayve’s teams to deploy, run, evaluate and continually improve machine-learning models. Processing petabytes of driving data across large GPU fleets, the team creates dependable, self-service capabilities that help model engineers understand model performance, improve quality and reduce operational effort and cost.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our Staff Software Engineer, you’ll own the platform’s technical vision and long-term direction. You’ll combine hands-on engineering with cross-team technical leadership, shaping how model engineering, infrastructure, compute and data capabilities come together to accelerate model development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧠 Your day-to-day</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the technical vision and architecture for the end-to-end Data Enrichment Platform, translating user needs into a clear technical direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the design, development and operation of backend services, APIs, model-execution workflows, versioned outputs, annotation capabilities and dataset catalogues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make architectural decisions for petabyte-scale data and large GPU fleets, addressing data locality, scheduling, capacity, backpressure, failure recovery, observability and cost.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Evaluate when to build, buy, reuse, integrate, consolidate or replace technologies as Wayve’s needs and the technology landscape evolve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish clear technical boundaries and ownership across model engineering, AI Platform, infrastructure, compute, storage and data teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Remain hands-on while leading cross-team delivery, mentoring senior engineers and raising standards for maintainable, tested and observable software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive adoption of reusable, self-service capabilities so teams can onboard and operate workflows independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define measurable service levels and success metrics covering reliability, throughput, cost, automation and adoption.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧩 What you’ll be working on</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A scalable platform for large-scale inference, automated evaluation, model monitoring, active learning and retraining.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-service backend services and APIs that enable dozens of model engineers to deploy and operate repeatable workflows independently.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reproducible dataset selection, versioned outputs, annotation workflows and dataset catalogues with clear metadata, provenance and lineage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reliable model-execution workflows operating across petabytes of driving data and large GPU fleets, scaling towards thousands of GPUs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitoring and operational tooling that make model quality, platform reliability, throughput, cost, runtime and workflow status visible.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The foundations for continuous evaluation, drift detection and automated model-improvement loops across robotics and computer-vision workloads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architectural improvements that reduce inference costs, duplicate compute and manual operational effort.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🙌 You should apply if</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have owned the long-term technical direction of a complex, multi-system platform or capability and can demonstrate the measurable outcomes of your decisions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong production software-engineering experience in Python, building maintainable, tested and observable backend services, APIs and data-processing systems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have deep experience designing and operating large-scale distributed systems for data-intensive or compute-intensive workloads.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have a track record of turning internal platforms into widely adopted, reliable and usable self-service products.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You bring excellent architecture and technology judgement, balancing immediate delivery needs with long-term platform direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You remain hands-on while leading delivery across organisational boundaries, influencing technical decisions and aligning teams around clear ownership and shared outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You communicate complex ideas clearly and have experience mentoring senior engineers and strengthening the technical capabilities of those around you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with workflow orchestration, batch inference, ML platforms, model deployment or registries would be an advantage. Relevant technologies include Flyte, Airflow, Dagster, Argo, Spark, Databricks, Ray, Kubernetes and GPU infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with annotation or dataset-catalogue platforms, including provenance, versioning, lineage and quality control, would also be valuable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with production robotics or computer-vision platforms—including annotation, inference, evaluation and model monitoring—is particularly desirable. Computer-vision research expertise is not required.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🌱 <strong>Not ticking every box? That’s totally okay!</strong> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re passionate about autonomy and the impact you could make at Wayve, we encourage you to apply even if you don’t meet every requirement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>More about Wayve</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 Wayve is building the leading AI platform for autonomous driving. We are pioneering an end-to-end AI approach that enables vehicles to learn directly from real-world experience, developing the ability to adapt, generalise and improve at scale. Instead of relying on hand-coded rules or pre-mapped environments, our AI Driver learns to drive by understanding the world around it. The result is technology that navigates complex urban environments with intelligence, precision and natural flow, unlocking meaningful advances in both safety and efficiency. We believe autonomy represents a once-in-a-generation transformation in how people and goods move, comparable to the shift from horses to cars, and from human-driven vehicles to intelligent machines.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our ambition is to make autonomy universal. Wayve’s mapless and hardware-agnostic AI platform integrates with global OEM partners, enabling continuous software evolution and unlocking advanced levels of automation from L2+ through to L4 as our core AI model scales. In a race increasingly defined by intelligence and real-world learning, Wayve is taking a distinct approach, building a generalisable driving intelligence that can power any vehicle, anywhere. By combining embodied AI with scalable deployment, we are creating technology that can be shaped to each OEM brand and driver experience, accelerating the transition to a safer, more intelligent future of mobility.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work 💻 — Locations &amp; Flexible Working</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in London. Our main hubs are in London, Sunnyvale, Yokohama, Herzliya, Vancouver and Leonberg. We operate a hybrid working model that combines in-person collaboration in our dedicated office spaces with focused time working remotely. This gives our teams the connection and energy of working together, alongside the flexibility to do their best work in a way that fits their lives.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🔍 The Interview Process</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our process is clear and respectful of your time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Initial call / Talent Partner screen</strong> (30 mins)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competency interviews:</strong> Python coding (60 mins), System design (60 mins)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Deep Dive Interviews:</strong> Technical Leadership, Hiring Manager interview (45 mins)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final interview:</strong> Mission, values and Staff-level calibration (45 mins)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ll always explain the format and work around your availability.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What’s in it for you (location dependent)</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Salaries benchmarked against the market annually</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📈 Meaningful equity, sharing in the ownership and long-term success of Wayve</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✈️ Relocation support and visa sponsorship where applicable</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">✅ Hybrid working, core hours and the chance to work hands-on in vehicle workshops and labs</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">📚 Learning and development budgets with support for training, conferences and growth</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Comprehensive benefits including health insurance, dental, enhanced maternity and paternity leave, retirement or pension where applicable, access to therapists, wellbeing partnerships, team socials and more</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">A quick, honest note before you apply.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Wayve is not a mature, fully-structured place with the playbook already written. Much of how we work is still being written, and if you join, you’ll help write it. That suits people who want real ownership more than people who need a settled structure from day one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If that sounds like the kind of problem you want to spend your time on, we’d really like to hear from you.<br /><br />At Wayve we're committed to creating a diverse, fair and respectful culture that is inclusive of everyone based on their unique skills and perspectives, and regardless of sex, race, religion or belief, ethnic or national origin, disability, age, citizenship, marital, domestic or civil partnership status, sexual orientation, gender identity, veteran status, pregnancy or related condition (including breastfeeding) or any other basis as protected by applicable law.<br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">For more information visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://wayve.ai/careers/">Careers at Wayve.</a> To learn more about what drives us, visit <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://wayve.ai/careers/">Values at Wayve</a><br /><br />DISCLAIMER: We will not ask about marriage or pregnancy, care responsibilities or disabilities in any of our job adverts or interviews. However, we do look to capture information about care responsibilities, and disabilities among other diversity information as part of an optional DEI Monitoring form to help us identify areas of improvement in our hiring process and ensure that the process is inclusive and non-discriminatory.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/wayve/staff-software-engineer-data-enrichment-platform-london-united-kingdom-26859","tags":["Simulation","Evaluation","Validation"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London, United Kingdom","created_at":1792431617},{"slug":"senior-data-remediation-project-manager-london-259943","company_name":"Delta Capita","title":"Senior Data Remediation Project Manager","description":"<p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Role - Senior Data Remediation Project Manager</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Location - London (Hybrid)</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Employment Type - 6 months FTC</span></strong></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Joining - Immediate</span></strong></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">About the Role:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">Delta Capita is seeking an experienced Senior Data Remediation Project Manager to lead a high-profile regulatory and customer remediation programme within the financial services sector. The successful candidate will be responsible for driving complex data remediation initiatives, coordinating multiple delivery workstreams, and ensuring the successful execution of large-scale remediation activities impacting customer data, operational processes, and technology landscapes.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#121317">This is a highly visible role requiring exceptional stakeholder management capabilities, strong programme governance experience, and a deep understanding of data, technology, and regulatory remediation environments.</span></p><p><br></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Key Responsibilities:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Lead the delivery of a large-scale data remediation programme within a regulated financial services environment.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Consolidate multiple data-related workstream plans into a single integrated delivery roadmap, ensuring clear dependencies, milestones, risks, and governance are maintained.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Drive execution across business, data, technology, operations, and change teams to ensure delivery objectives are met.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Engage and influence senior stakeholders, including Executive leadership, Programme Sponsors, Risk, Compliance, Technology, and Operations teams.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Assess and manage data remediation impacts across systems, data architecture, operating models, controls, and manual processes.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Provide strong programme governance, tracking delivery progress, risks, issues, and remediation plans.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Identify opportunities to leverage AI and emerging technologies to improve remediation effectiveness, customer outcomes, and operational efficiency.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Collaborate with technical teams to understand data lineage, data quality issues, system dependencies, and remediation approaches.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Ensure remediation activities are aligned with regulatory expectations, governance standards, and customer outcome requirements.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Support decision-making through robust reporting, stakeholder communications, and programme documentation.<br><br></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Required Experience:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Proven experience leading large-scale data remediation or regulatory remediation programmes within financial services.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Strong project or programme management background with experience delivering complex, multi-workstream initiatives.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Demonstrated ability to manage senior stakeholders and operate effectively within highly visible and regulated environments.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Strong understanding of data remediation methodologies, data quality management, and data governance principles.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Experience working across business, technology, data, and operational teams.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Good understanding of technology architecture, system landscapes, data flows, and remediation impacts.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Ability to build and manage integrated delivery plans across multiple parallel workstreams.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Experience managing programme risks, dependencies, governance forums, and regulatory scrutiny.</span></p> <br> <p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Desirable Experience:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Experience delivering customer remediation programmes within banking, lending, or retail financial services organisations.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Knowledge of regulatory remediation, customer data management, conduct risk, or operational risk frameworks.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Experience working on large-scale customer contact and claims remediation programmes, including PPI, complaints remediation, redress, or similar customer outcome initiatives.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Understanding of AI use cases, automation opportunities, and advanced analytics within remediation and operational environments.</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Exposure to data lineage, data governance, and enterprise data management programmes.<br><br></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Key Skills:</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Data Remediation</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Regulatory Remediation</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Programme &amp; Project Management</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Senior Stakeholder Management</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Data Governance &amp; Data Quality</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Delivery Planning &amp; Execution</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Risk &amp; Issue Management</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Financial Services Transformation</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• AI &amp; Innovation</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Technology &amp; Data Architecture Awareness</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Customer Remediation Programmes</span></p><p><span style="color:#121317">• Change Management<br><br></span></p><p><strong><span style="color:#121317">Why Join Delta Capita?</span></strong></p><p><span st