lexibility to spend on the benefits that matter most to you.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Learning &amp; development</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A growing personal L&amp;D budget</strong> (starting at £500 per year and increasing with tenure to £3,000 per year).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Dedicated L&amp;D or volunteering time:</strong> one paid day every quarter to invest in your development or support a cause you care about.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlimited access to our internal Academy:</strong> including courses, learning resources and professional certifications.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Community and Inclusion</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are committed to creating a workplace that is free from discrimination and bias, and where everyone has equal opportunities to succeed and contribute. We acknowledge that our work here is never done - and we promise to continue striving for inclusivity every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Encouraging diverse backgrounds and unique perspectives, applications are welcomed regardless of whether every listed requirement is fully met.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/pmmalliance/b2b-sponsorship-partnerships-executive-london-83402","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hybrid","created_at":1792420816},{"slug":"member-of-technical-staff-emea-london-491354","company_name":"Fireworks","title":"Member of Technical Staff (EMEA)","description":"<h2><strong>About Us:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fireworks is the platform for specialized intelligence, enabling companies to build, train, and serve AI models tailored to their own data, workflows, and products. Founded by the team behind PyTorch and backed by AMD, Atreides, Benchmark Capital, Index Ventures, Lightspeed, NVIDIA, Sequoia Capital, and TCV, Fireworks powers production AI with hundreds of state-of-the-art open models across text, image, embedding, audio, and multimodal workloads. Today, Fireworks is a Series D company valued at $17.5 billion, bringing together an ambitious, collaborative team that's building the future of enterprise AI.</p><h2><strong>The Role:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />As a Member of Technical Staff on the EMEA field team, you build on top of one of the largest inference platforms in the world. The work spans the stack: capabilities on top of inference and serving, tooling around fine-tuning and post-training of LLMs, and the product our region’s customers need that the core platform team will not take on. You are first and foremost an excellent software engineer; that is what we are testing for. You prefer building product to being customer-facing, and that is exactly right for this role, though you are welcome to join customer work when it interests you.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Treat this as a flexible role: a bucket for exceptional builders at different levels of experience rather than a fixed job spec. There is no specific seniority requirement; anywhere from 3 to 10 years of experience can fit.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">What we value most is first principles thinking: reasoning about unfamiliar problems from the ground up rather than from playbooks. You will be evaluated on this directly in the interview process, and strength here can outweigh gaps elsewhere in your background.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities: </strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build: Design and ship product capabilities end to end, from ambiguous need to running in production.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build on Inference: Create capabilities on top of the serving stack: routing, model controls, observability, and whatever a deployment turns out to need.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build on Training: Ship tooling around fine-tuning and post-training of LLMs, from data pipelines to evaluation, working alongside our applied ML engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own Regional Capability: Turn EMEA-specific requirements into product, working with core platform where the line is unclear.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineering Quality: Set the engineering bar for the regional team; your code is the reference.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agentic Development: Use coding agents and AI tooling as a core part of how you build, with judgment about when to trust the output.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optional Customer Work: Join deployments or customer conversations when useful or interesting; never required.<br /></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Minimum Qualifications:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First principles and critical thinking: the ability to break down novel problems and reason to a solution without a reference implementation. This is the primary interview signal and can outweigh other qualifications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent software engineering: depth in backend systems and infrastructure, and a track record of shipping production systems you owned.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong coding skills in Python and at least one systems language.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in AI-assisted and agentic engineering: uses coding agents and AI tooling as a core part of how you build, and knows when to trust the output and when not to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Genuine interest in inference and AI infrastructure.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><h2><strong>Why Fireworks?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solve Hard Problems: Tackle challenges at the forefront of AI infrastructure, from low-latency inference to scalable model serving.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build What’s Next: Work with bleeding-edge technology that impacts how businesses and developers harness AI globally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership &amp; Impact: Join a fast-growing, passionate team where your work directly shapes the future of AI—no bureaucracy, just results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn from the Best: Collaborate with world-class engineers and AI researchers who thrive on curiosity and innovation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Fireworks AI is an equal-opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all innovators.</em></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/fireworks/member-of-technical-staff-emea-london-491354","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792420816},{"slug":"ai-deployment-strategist-emea-london-351275","company_name":"Fireworks","title":"AI Deployment Strategist (EMEA)","description":"<h2><strong>About Us:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fireworks is the platform for specialized intelligence, enabling companies to build, train, and serve AI models tailored to their own data, workflows, and products. Founded by the team behind PyTorch and backed by AMD, Atreides, Benchmark Capital, Index Ventures, Lightspeed, NVIDIA, Sequoia Capital, and TCV, Fireworks powers production AI with hundreds of state-of-the-art open models across text, image, embedding, audio, and multimodal workloads. Today, Fireworks is a Series D company valued at $17.5 billion, bringing together an ambitious, collaborative team that's building the future of enterprise AI.</p><h2><strong>The Role: </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />As an AI Deployment Strategist, you are the long-term owner of our most important customer accounts. You pair with Account Executives to close: scoping pilots, setting success criteria, and running the technical side of the commercial conversation. At signature, you take the account and stay on it, driving adoption and expansion over years rather than quarters, so AEs can move to the next deal. This role suits entrepreneurial, technically credible operators; founder and founder CEO backgrounds are a strong fit.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What we value most is first principles thinking: reasoning about unfamiliar problems from the ground up rather than from playbooks. You will be evaluated on this directly in the interview process, and strength here can outweigh gaps elsewhere in your background.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key Responsibilities:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Account Ownership: Own the customer relationship and commercial outcome from signature onward, including adoption, expansion, and renewals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deal Support: Partner with AEs pre-signature on pilot scoping, success criteria, and technical-commercial framing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Delivery Cadence: Run the operating rhythm of the account across the customer's and Fireworks' teams (FDEs, AMLEs, product, support).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Value Realization: Translate customer goals into concrete deployment milestones and make sure they land.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expansion Strategy: Identify and drive new workloads, teams, and use cases within existing accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Voice of Customer: Represent account needs internally with enough technical precision to be actionable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Minimum Qualifications:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First principles and critical thinking: the ability to break down novel problems and reason to a solution without a reference implementation. This is the primary interview signal and can outweigh other qualifications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent technical depth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years in roles combining technical substance with commercial ownership (deployment strategy, technical consulting, founder, forward deployed, or similar).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong technical credibility: able to hold your own with customer engineering leadership and our field engineers, and to reason about AI infrastructure tradeoffs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of owning outcomes over long horizons, not handing off after the sale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent judgment, communication, and stakeholder management with senior audiences.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Preferred Qualifications:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founder or founding team experience, especially as CEO or commercial lead of a technical product.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience deploying or operating AI/ML products in production with enterprise customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience navigating enterprise constraints in EMEA (procurement, data residency, GDPR, EU AI Act).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in a startup or fast-paced environment.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Why Fireworks?</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Solve Hard Problems: Tackle challenges at the forefront of AI infrastructure, from low-latency inference to scalable model serving.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build What’s Next: Work with bleeding-edge technology that impacts how businesses and developers harness AI globally.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ownership &amp; Impact: Join a fast-growing, passionate team where your work directly shapes the future of AI—no bureaucracy, just results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn from the Best: Collaborate with world-class engineers and AI researchers who thrive on curiosity and innovation.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Fireworks AI is an equal-opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all innovators.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/fireworks/ai-deployment-strategist-emea-london-351275","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792420816},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-new-products-london-31951","company_name":"Airwallex","title":"Senior Software Engineer, New Products","description":"<h2><strong>About Airwallex</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Airwallex is the AI-native financial operating system for a real-time, intelligent economy. More than 675,000 businesses, including McLaren Racing, Qantas, SHEIN, and TikTok, use us, directly or through our platform partners, to run their financial operations or build and monetize financial products of their own.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We started in Melbourne in 2015 to build the infrastructure global commerce runs on. We're the regulated backbone behind global payments: not by accident, but by design. A decade plus, 85+ licenses, and a financial infrastructure spanning North America, Europe, the Middle East, and Asia-Pacific.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're co-headquartered in San Francisco and Singapore, with more than 2,300 people across 27 offices. We hire builders with founder-level energy, people who move fast with good judgment, dig in with real curiosity, and make calls from first principles rather than waiting to be told what to do. Read our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.airwallex.com/en-us/operating-principles"> <u>operating principles</u></a> to see it in full.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring Location: </strong> London (Hybrid Mode)</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Total Compensation: </strong>140,000 to 200,000 GBP </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>How you'll make impact</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Founders’ Lab turns ambitious, ambiguous ideas into financial products that can be tested with real users. You’ll combine software engineering and product judgement to move from executive vision to working software quickly, with ownership across the full product lifecycle.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner directly with the CEO and global leadership to turn strategic visions and disruptive AI capabilities into functional, market-ready financial software in weeks, not quarters.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape product direction by synthesising business requirements, regulatory realities, user needs and emerging technology. You won’t just build to a specification — you’ll help define what to build and why.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run rapid proofs of concept, deploy products to live users, test market fit and balance fast iteration with sound technical foundations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver end-to-end solutions across the stack, from backend architecture and API design through to frontend polish, putting useful products in the hands of global users.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build clean, maintainable software from ambiguous executive direction, with complete end-to-end ownership across both product and engineering.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work from our London office three days a week.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What we're looking for</h2><h3>Essentials</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">6+ years of software engineering experience, with a strong foundation in backend architecture and the ability to work confidently across the full stack when needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of personally shipping products from scratch in a high-growth startup, corporate innovation lab or greenfield environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong product and commercial judgement, with the ability to challenge assumptions and evaluate technical decisions through the lens of user experience and business impact.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A pragmatic, resourceful approach to problem-solving, with a track record of finding creative paths around institutional and technical roadblocks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfort working with high ambiguity and translating high-level strategic or executive direction into clean, maintainable software.</p></li></ul><h3>Preferred</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building software that uses generative AI, large language models or intelligent workflow automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in fintech, payments, compliance or money-movement infrastructure.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience as a startup founder, founding engineer or technical lead of a rapid-prototyping team.</p></li></ul><h2>You'll thrive here if</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own the outcome and you don't wait for permission to fix what's broken.</p></li><li