<li><strong>Private health insurance</strong> - via Vitality</li>
<li><strong>Bike subscription</strong> – £30/month discount towards Bike Club subscription</li>
</ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/bike-club/founders-associate-london-342424","tags":["Business Operations"],"job_types":["Permanent employment contract (open-ended contract)","entry"],"location":"London","created_at":1792414901},{"slug":"commodity-pricing-engine-developer-london-347532","company_name":"Market Cloud","title":"Commodity Pricing Engine Developer/Murex Developer","description":"<h2>About the Role</h2><p>We are seeking a highly skilled Commodity Pricing Engine Developer to design, build, and enhance a bespoke pricing engine that generates real-time prices for client RFQ (Request for Quote) workflows. The ideal candidate will have deep expertise in commodity derivatives pricing, quantitative model development, and software engineering, with a strong focus on delivering accurate and low-latency pricing solutions in trading environments.</p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul><li>Design, develop, and maintain pricing models for commodity and OTC derivatives products.</li><li>Build, calibrate, and validate quantitative pricing models to ensure accuracy and robustness.</li><li>Develop and enhance a bespoke pricing engine for RFQ quote generation.</li><li>Integrate pricing models with market data feeds, trading platforms, and RFQ systems.</li><li>Optimize pricing calculations for real-time performance and low-latency execution.</li><li>Collaborate with traders, quants, and technology teams to translate business requirements into scalable solutions.</li><li>Conduct model testing, performance analysis, and continuous improvements.</li><li>Ensure compliance with model governance, validation standards, and risk management frameworks.</li><li>Support production deployments and troubleshoot pricing-related issues.</li></ul><h2>Required Skills & Experience</h2><ul><li>Strong experience in Commodity Derivatives or OTC Derivatives Pricing.</li><li>Proven expertise in Quantitative Development, including model creation, calibration, and validation.</li><li>Deep understanding of financial mathematics and derivatives valuation techniques.</li><li>Strong software engineering skills with proficiency in:</li><li>Python</li><li>C++</li><li>Java</li><li>Similar object-oriented programming languages</li><li>Experience integrating pricing systems with market data and trading platforms.</li><li>Strong problem-solving and analytical skills.</li><li>Ability to work effectively in a fast-paced trading environment.</li></ul><h2>Preferred Qualifications</h2><ul><li>Experience building real-time pricing engines within electronic trading (e-Trading) environments.</li><li>Knowledge of Bloomberg market data integration.</li><li>Experience with messaging technologies and connectivity frameworks.</li><li>Familiarity with distributed systems and high-performance computing concepts.</li><li>Understanding of commodity markets, trading workflows, and risk management processes.</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/market-cloud/commodity-pricing-engine-developer-london-347532","tags":["Software Development"],"job_types":["Permanent employment contract (open-ended contract)","professional / experienced"],"location":"London","created_at":1792428450},{"slug":"senior-designer-london-441009","company_name":"Tangible","title":"Senior Designer","description":"<h2>About Tangible</h2><p>Tangible Markets builds secondary market infrastructure for private fund LP interests. Our platforms help investors, wealth managers, fund managers and lenders buy, sell, price, finance and close secondary transactions. Our products:</p><p><strong>Liquidity Hub:</strong> a secondary marketplace where LPs list fund interests and qualified buyers bid, with liquidity windows, tender offers and NAV lending.</p><p><strong>Auctions:</strong> a competitive sale process for fund interests, supported by pricing models, pricing reports and market sentiment data.</p><p><strong>Closing Platform:</strong> a transaction workflow built with a leading law firm to manage transfer documents, signatures and closing steps.</p><h2>The role</h2><p>You own the design of our products end to end, from research to shipped UI. You work with product, engineering and data teams on complex financial workflows used by institutional buyers, wealth advisors, lenders, fund managers and lawyers. Several products run as white-label versions for large financial partners.<br><br>Position open to candidates based in the EU and the UK.</p><h2>Responsibilities</h2><ul><li><p>Own visual branding and design direction across every product, with a modern and consistent standard.</p></li><li><p>Lead the UX and UI revamp across the whole platform.</p></li><li><p>Design end-to-end flows across all products: onboarding, listings, bidding, pricing, financing and closing.</p></li><li><p>Turn complex financial and legal processes into clear, simple interfaces.</p></li><li><p>Design data-dense screens: pricing outputs, dashboards, reports, tables and comparisons.</p></li><li><p>Run user research and usability testing with buyers, sellers, advisors and partners.</p></li><li><p>Own the design system across products and white-label client versions.</p></li><li><p>Own the design process, including where AI tools fit to speed up research, prototyping and production.</p></li><li><p>Own design organization: files, handoff, and how work moves from design to build.</p></li><li><p>Set the quality bar and hold it. Nothing ships that has not cleared it.</p></li><li><p>Direct the product designer and review their output.</p></li><li><p>Work with engineering through build and QA so designs ship as intended.</p></li></ul><h2>Requirements</h2><ul><li><p>6+ years of product design experience, including 3+ years on complex B2B, fintech or enterprise products.</p></li><li><p>Deep UX skills: information architecture, interaction design, user research and usability testing.</p></li><li><p>Proven experience building and maintaining a design system in Figma: components, tokens, variants and documentation.</p></li><li><p>Daily use of AI productivity tools in design work (for example Claude, Figma AI, v0 or Cursor) to prototype and iterate fast.</p></li><li><p>Experience designing multi-step, multi-role workflows with permissions, statuses and approvals.</p></li><li><p>Experience with multi-tenant or white-label products.</p></li><li><p>Working knowledge of front-end basics (HTML, CSS, component libraries) and how designs translate to code.</p></li><li><p>Strong written and verbal communication, with the ability to explain design decisions to business and tech teams.</p></li><li><p>A portfolio showing process, trade-offs and shipped work.</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul><li><p>Knowledge of private markets, secondaries, wealth management or capital markets.</p></li><li><p>Experience in regulated industries: compliance flows, audit trails, disclosures and e-signature.</p></li><li><p>Accessibility knowledge (WCAG).</p></li></ul><p></p><p>Please submit your resume, portfolio, and a brief cover letter explaining your experience and why you want to join Tangible. Portfolios are reviewed before interviews are scheduled, so make sure yours is up to date.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/tangible/senior-designer-london-441009","tags":["Remote","Media","Screen and Web Design"],"job_types":["Self-employed contractor (freelancer)","freelance","professional / experienced"],"location":"London","created_at":1792411282},{"slug":"senior-consumer-duty-specialist-london-121450","company_name":"Pleo","title":"Senior Consumer Duty Specialist","description":"<h2><strong>About Pleo</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Messy spend management is tricky business. And tedious processes are a lose-lose situation for all involved, not just finance. At Pleo, we're changing that. We build spend solutions that make managing money seamless, empowering, and surprisingly effective for finance teams and employees alike - with a vision to help all businesses ‘go beyond’.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The word ‘Pleo’ actually means ‘more than you’d expect’, and living by that mantra has been the secret to our success over the last 10 years.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Now, we’re at a pivotal moment in our journey; every move we make has a direct impact on our 40,000+ customers, our business, and our collective success. We need people who take pride in uncovering customer needs, who turn complex problems into simple solutions, challenge the way things are done (respectfully), and always aim high. With great ambitions driving us forward, we can’t say we’ve got this whole thing figured out. And frankly, that’s half the fun! What we can say is that we’re a driven, progressive, and, importantly, a kind bunch of 850+ people from over 100 nationalities, all committed to delivering the future of business spending, together.</p><h2><strong>About the role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role, you will play a central part in assessing, questioning, and enhancing how customers experience Pleo. Drawing on deep regulatory knowledge, you will lead Consumer Duty initiatives, actively spot potential customer harm, examine what drives customer journeys, and ensure targeted remediation creates lasting, positive impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll need sharp analytical skills and the confidence to influence stakeholders, translating data and MI into decisive action. You will construct and manage dashboards and reporting mechanisms that illuminate emerging patterns, vulnerable customer risks, and key concerns, offering executive leadership clear visibility into operational gaps and necessary solutions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your contribution goes well beyond producing MI. You will conduct QA across complex complaint handling and sensitive customer interactions, manage Ombudsman cases, and speak up when evidence shows outcomes aren't meeting expectations. Collaborating across teams, you'll turn data-driven insights into practical improvements, drive projects to completion, and evaluate whether changes deliver real results for our users.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're seeking someone who views Consumer Duty as a powerful driver of business improvement rather than a routine compliance exercise. You'll bring together technical understanding, rigorous analysis, and constructive challenge to investigate root causes, align key partners, deliver change, and prove that customer experiences are continuously getting better.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Who you’ll be working with and reporting to </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll work closely with teams across Customer Support, Complaints, Compliance, Risk, Operations, Product, Data, Technology, and other business functions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role will have broad exposure across the organisation, particularly when customer outcome risks or Consumer Duty-related remediation require cross-functional action.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll also work closely with senior stakeholders through Consumer Duty governance and reporting, helping translate detailed analysis into clear insights, risks, recommendations, and actions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you’ll be doing</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Consumer Duty Specialist, you will:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn data into customer outcome insight</strong>: Build and own MI, dashboards, KPIs, and reporting that give the business a clear view of customer outcomes, trends, risks, and emerging areas of concern.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own Consumer Duty reporting</strong>: Produce monthly and quarterly Consumer Duty reporting, turning complex data into a clear story for senior leadership and Board-level audiences. You'll go beyond showing <em>what</em> happened to explain <em>why it matters</em> and <em>what we should do about it</em>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Identify customer harm</strong>: Use complaints, QA findings, customer feedback, vulnerable customer data, Ombudsman cases, and MI to identify potential customer harm, emerging risks, and systemic issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Challenge the business</strong>: Where the evidence suggests customers aren't receiving good outcomes, you'll be expected to ask difficult questions, challenge assumptions, and ensure the issue is properly understood and addressed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Drive remediation and change</strong>: Work with stakeholders across the business to agree remediation plans, establish clear owners and timelines, and help drive Consumer Duty-related projects and improvements through to completion.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Provide complaints QA</strong>: Conduct weekly quality reviews of complaints handled by the Complaints Manager, using findings to identify quality issues, customer risks, and wider trends.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Manage Ombudsman activity</strong>: Act as the primary operational contact with the UK Ombudsman, managing referred complaints, responses, remedies, compensation, invoices, and related communications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Leverage AI and smart automation</strong>: Spot opportunities to apply automated tools and AI to scale and streamline Consumer Duty analytics, monitoring, and workflows. You will feel empowered to test emerging tech and eliminate repetitive manual work, maintaining proper critical evaluation and human governance whenever compliance risks or customer impacts are involved.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you bring</strong> </h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll thrive in this role if you have:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong Consumer Duty knowledge</strong>: You understand the principles of Consumer Duty and how they translate into practical customer outcomes, particularly across complaints, customer support, vulnerable customers, and customer journeys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong data and MI experience</strong>: You know how to take complex data, build meaningful dashboards and reporting, and identify the insights that actually matter. You're comfortable working with data rather than simply consuming reports created by others.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A customer outcome mindset</strong>: You're naturally curious about how customers are experiencing the business and are able to connect data, customer feedback, complaints, and operational activity to real customer outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong analytical and problem-solving skills</strong>: You can spot trends, anomalies, and patterns, investigate root causes, and determine whether an issue is isolated or potentially systemic.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The confidence to challenge</strong>: You're comfortable questioning decisions, processes, and assumptions when the evidence suggests customers may be experiencing poor outcomes. You can challenge constructively and build relationships at the same time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A bias towards action</strong>: You don't believe reporting is the end of the process. You want to understand what needs to change, bring people together, and help make it happen.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Project and remediation experience</strong>: You're comfortable managing actions, timelines, dependencies, stakeholders, and risks across cross-functional projects, particularly where there is a regulatory, customer, or operational outcome to deliver.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>An AI and automation mindset</strong>: You're naturally curious about how AI and automation can make processes more efficient, improve analysis, and free up time for higher-value work. You look for sensible opportunities to automate repetitive tasks and use AI to augment your thinking, while maintaining appropriate human oversight, critical judgement, and accountability — particularly where customer outcomes or regulatory decisions are involved.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>Why is this role a good fit for you</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is a good fit for you if:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You love using data to uncover things that others might not see.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want your analysis to drive real change, rather than sit in a report or dashboard.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy asking <em>"why?"</em> and getting to the root cause of customer problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable challenging the business when the evidence tells you something isn't working.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is not a good fit for you if:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prefer to produce reporting without being involved in what happens afterwards.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're uncomfortable challenging stakeholders or having difficult conversations when customer outcomes aren't where they should be.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prefer working within a narrow functional remit rather than across multiple teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2><strong>How you’ll develop in this role </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">In your first 6 months at Pleo, you'll:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build a deep understanding of our customer outcome data, existing Consumer Duty MI, complaints, vulnerable customer journeys, and current areas of risk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of key Consumer Duty dashboards and reporting, developing a clear view of the metrics and insights that matter most.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish strong relationships with stakeholders across Customer Support, Complaints, Compliance, Risk, Operations, Product, Data, and Technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead the analysis behind Consumer Duty reporting and help shape how customer outcomes are presented to senior stakeholders and the Board.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Over time, you'll have the opportunity to shape how Pleo measures, understands, and improves customer outcomes, helping move Consumer Duty from a regulatory obligation into a genuine driver of better customer experiences and better business decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Show me the benefits!</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your own Pleo card (no more out-of-pocket spending!)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch is on us for your work days - enjoy catered meals or receive a lunch allowance based on your local office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive private healthcare - depending on your location, coverage options include Vitality, Alan or Médis</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer 25 days of holiday + your public holidays</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For our Team, we offer both hybrid and fully remote working options</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Option to purchase 5 additional days of holiday through a salary sacrifice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use MyndUp to give our employees access to free mental health and well-being support with great success so far</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Paid parental leave - we want to make sure that we're supportive of families and help you feel that you don't have to compromise your family due to work</p></li></ul><h2><strong><br />The interview process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We want to ensure you are set-up for success and understand what will be expected of you. If your application is successful, our interview process is as follows:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Intro call: A 30-minute chat with our Talent Partner to discuss the role and your background.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meet the Hiring Manager: 1hr going through role in more depth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pleo Challenge: A case study were you talk us through how you'd solve a work appropriate challenge.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Transparency is important to us so we also wanted to share some insights about what we’re looking for in applications to ensure you can set yourself up for success!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Last time we advertised this role, we received a really high volume of applications but could only select so many. Some of the key reasons why previous candidates didn’t make it past the application screening stage include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">CV writing and content: we receive a lot of CVs, and many of them are AI-generated. We love seeing people leverage AI—it’s a big focus for us internally too—but without human intervention, these CVs can sometimes become generic and fail to show a candidate in the best light. What we're really looking for is the specific details of real impact that only you know from your previous experience. A top tip from us is to use the “Achieved X, as measured by Y, by doing Z” formula (credit: Laszlo Bock, ~2014) to give a really clear picture of what you’ve worked on. A final note: including links to your previous companies' websites is a huge help and allows us to truly understand your background!</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Application care: every single application we receive is reviewed by a human (yes, hundreds of them) because we believe that candidates' efforts should be matched by an equal level of human care. This means that we expect a similar level of attention put into your application. Read and answer the application questions carefully, they make a huge difference in our decision-making process.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Profile to role fit: highlight most important aspects of the role, points that might get misunderstood, any specific industry requirements etc.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About your application</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>English first.</strong> Since it's our company language, please submit your application in English. You’ll be using it a lot if you join us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A fair look for everyone.</strong> Our talent team reads every single application to ensure the process is fair. To keep things running smoothly, we only accept applications through our system—our support team can’t pass on calls or emails.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Diversity drives us.</strong> We can only reach our goals if our team reflects the world around us. That starts with you hitting apply, even if you don't tick every single box. We encourage people from all backgrounds and experiences to join us.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Interview at your best.</strong> We want you to feel comfortable throughout the process. If you have any accessibility requirements or need a specific format, email ----- We’ll design a process that works for you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your data is safe.</strong> When you apply, we process your personal data as a data processor. For more information on how Pleo processes personal data, read our Privacy Policy <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" class="in-cell-link" href="https://www.pleo.io/en/legal"><u>here</u></a>.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Applying for multiple roles?</strong> Nothing is stopping you, and we assess every role independently. However, we do look for alignment, so make sure you can explain why your interest and experience are right for each specific role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reapplying.</strong> If you’re applying for the same role again, please wait six months from your last decision before hitting submit.</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/pleo/senior-consumer-duty-specialist-london-121450","tags":["Legal"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792410016},{"slug":"web-engineer-intern-london-436997","company_name":"Epicgames","title":"Web Engineer Intern","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;WHAT MAKES US EPIC?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the core of Epic’s success are talented, passionate people. Epic prides itself on creating a collaborative, welcoming, and creative environment. Whether it’s building award-winning games or crafting engine technology that enables others to make visually stunning interactive experiences, we’re always innovating.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Being Epic means being a part of a team that continually strives to do right by our community and users. We’re constantly innovating to raise the bar of engine and game development.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ENGINEERING - EPIC GAMES SERVICES&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Driving the plug-in power behind Unreal Engine 5. We bridge connections for licensees and our own internal game teams to online services. This allows games like Fortnite to utilize a combination of platform online services as well as Epic’s own online services to build cross-platform online features. Login, parties, voice chat, matchmaking, purchasing, cloud storage, and analytics are just a few examples of online features that our Online Game Services team helps games utilize.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;WEB ENGINEER INTERN&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Web Engineer Intern to join the Tools &amp;amp; Portals team within Epic Online Services. Tools &amp;amp; Portals builds the software, platforms, and digital experiences that enable Epic’s internal teams, player support operations, players, and external developers to work with and access Epic services more effectively. You will contribute to production systems across the full stack while gaining hands-on experience with modern web development, backend services, cloud infrastructure, and AI-assisted software development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build full-stack features using React, Next.js, TypeScript, and Tailwind CSS with guidance from the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Contribute to development of backend services and APIs using Next.js, NestJS, and Node.js&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Learn and apply development practices for production infrastructure including AWS, Kubernetes, containers, and CI/CD pipelines&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Write, test, review, and deploy production code alongside experienced engineers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Learn and apply AI-assisted software development workflows throughout the software development lifecycle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Contribute to internal tools and developer-facing platforms used across Epic Games&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Interest in full-stack web development and learning modern engineering technologies&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Some familiarity with JavaScript, TypeScript, React, or similar web technologies through coursework, projects, or previous experience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Eagerness to learn, ask questions, and contribute to solving well-defined engineering problems&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Willingness to explore new technologies and codebases, seek support when needed, and incorporate feedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Ability to work effectively with guidance, communicate questions and blockers, and incorporate feedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Strong collaboration skills and willingness to work closely with engineers, product partners, external teams, and stakeholders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Understanding of defined requirements and willingness to ask clarifying questions when needed&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Strong communication and collaboration skills, including sharing progress and incorporating feedback&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span&gt;Interest in using AI tools and AI-assisted workflows as part of software development&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;This internship has a flexible start date in 2027. Recruitment will be ongoing until teams find an ideal match. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the posting location for the duration of the internship. For more information about Epic’s Early Career Program, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epicgames.com/site/en-US/earlycareers&quot;&gt;epicgames.com/earlycareers&lt;/a&gt;. This is going to be Epic!&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h2&gt;ABOUT US&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic Games​ ​is a leading interactive entertainment company. For over 30 years we&#39;ve been making award-winning games and engine technology that empowers others to make visually stunning games and 3D content that bring environments to life like never before. Epic&#39;s award-winning Unreal Engine technology not only provides game developers the ability to build high-fidelity, interactive experiences for PC, console, mobile, and VR, it is also a tool being embraced by content creators across a variety of industries such as media and entertainment, automotive, and architectural design. As we continue to build our Engine technology and develop remarkable games, we strive to build teams of world-class talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Like what you hear? Come be a part of something Epic!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Epic Games deeply values diverse teams and an inclusive work culture, and we are proud to be an Equal Opportunity employer. Learn more about our Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Policy &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epicgames.com/site/en-US/eeo-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Note to Recruitment Agencies: &lt;/strong&gt;Epic does not accept any unsolicited resumes or approaches from any unauthorized third party (including recruitment or placement agencies) (i.e., a third party with whom we do not have a negotiated and validly executed agreement). We will not pay any fees to any unauthorized third party. Further details on these matters can be found &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.epicgames.com/note-to-recruitment-agencies&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/epicgames/web-engineer-intern-london-436997","tags":["Engineering Specialist"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1792400113},{"slug":"senior-engagement-manager-london-435445","company_name":"Legora","title":"Senior Engagement Manager","description":"<h2>About Us</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Legora is redefining how legal work gets done. Not built for lawyers, built with them. We work alongside the world’s best legal teams, who expect excellence, precision, and speed, and we hold ourselves to the same bar.<br /><br />Our AI-native workspace lets legal professionals move faster, think more clearly, and operate with sharper precision. By analysing thousands of documents in minutes and powering end-to-end workflows, we cut through complexity, teams can focus on what matters: judgment, strategy, and outcomes.<br /><br />2,100+ customers across 80+ countries trust us, including Cleary Gottlieb, Goodwin, Linklaters, White &amp; Case, Dentons, and Barclays. We’ve scaled to<strong> $200M+ in ARR</strong>, with teams across Europe, North America and APAC, and continue to expand through acquisitions including Qura, Walter AI, Graceview, Cadastral, and Wexler.<br /><br />We partner with world-class performers: including Aaron Judge and the New York Yankees, Ludvig Åberg (and his caddie), and campaigns featuring Jude Law.<br /><br />Joining Legora means three things.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>lean in: </strong>ownership over titles, outcomes over intentions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We <strong>fight for excellence:</strong> high standards, direct, ego-free feedback.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We<strong> grow together:</strong> as a team and with our customers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission before ego. Everyone contributes. No one coasts.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you’re driven by impact, pace, and raising the bar. This is the place.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />The way legal work gets done is changing, and Engagement is at the centre of that transformation. We're looking for an experienced Engagement Manager to own Legora's global relationship with one of the Big 4, one of our most significant partnerships, and to fundamentally change the way that firm works with Legora.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a role for someone who has led change inside large, complex organisations and knows that real transformation is designed and managed. You will own the adoption and long-term success of this client globally: building the relationships, defining the outcomes and serving as the trusted adviser and orchestrator who turns Legora into an embedded part of how their teams operate.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Global means global. You will set the strategy for how the firm adopts Legora worldwide, and Engagement Managers in other regions will run their local programmes against the direction and decisions you set. Day to day, you will be the point of contact for the firm's UK and Ireland practice from our London office, and you will travel regularly to other<br />member firms in the network to build those relationships and land the programme on the ground. Expect to be travelling around 25% of the time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At the heart of the role is designing the client's adoption playbook and delivering a multi-year change-management programme that transforms how they work. You will build the roadmap, sequence initiatives from initial rollout through firm-wide scaled adoption, define measurable outcomes and ROI and evolve the programme as new AI capabilities and use cases emerge.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be critical as we continue to build a best-in-class adoption programme at Legora, helping the client realise measurable ROI, expand successful use cases and transform the way their teams work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You'll Do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You'll own the global relationship end to end, leading the post-sale experience across every member firm we work with. Specifically, you will:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />● Set the global adoption strategy for the account and lead its execution across regions. Engagement Managers in other markets will deliver their local programmes against the strategy and decisions you set, and you will be accountable for coherence and outcomes globally.<br />● Act as the primary point of contact for the firm's UK and Ireland practice, while travelling frequently to other member firms to build senior relationships and support local delivery in person.<br />● Design the client's adoption playbook: the tailored change-management approach, stakeholder map and target outcomes for how the firm adopts Legora and transforms the way it works.<br />● Execute against that playbook, sequencing initiatives from initial rollout to enterprise-wide scaled adoption and adapting as the client's needs and Legora's capabilities evolve.<br />● Act as a strategic adviser who deeply understands the client's goals and legal and professional services workflows, surfaces high-impact opportunities and guides teams towards maximum value from Legora.<br />● Drive sustained value through a structured operating cadence: success plans, enablement, stakeholder check-ins, training and value reviews.<br />● Orchestrate engagement from cross-functional teams to accelerate client success (GTM, Product, Legal Engineering, Engineering, Marketing, Support), maintaining end-to-end account context and coordination globally.<br />● Partner with GTM on key commercial moments to ensure seamless transitions, continuity and exceptional customer experience, and to identify and realise expansion opportunities across the account.<br />● Translate customer feedback into action by collaborating closely with Product, Engineering and Marketing to inform roadmap, positioning and enablement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You care deeply about customer outcomes and you know that transformation has to be designed and led. You're proactive, strategic and comfortable steering demanding, senior stakeholders through significant change. You take pride in being the reason customers adopt, grow and succeed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We're looking for:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />● 5+ years experience in management consulting, legal, LegalTech or customer success in an AI-native B2B vertical.<br />● Extensive experience working with or inside a Big 4 firm is highly desirable, we want someone who already understands how these firms are structured, how decisions get made and how change actually lands across member firms.<br />● A consulting or transformation background, with a demonstrated track record of designing and delivering change-management programmes inside large, complex organisations.<br />● Experience building tailored transformation roadmaps and adoption plans and steering them to measurable outcomes.<br />● A track record of driving adoption, retention and satisfaction with enterprise clients and senior stakeholders.<br />● Experience leading through influence rather than direct authority. You will set the direction that colleagues in other regions deliver against, so you need to be able to bring people with you.<br />● Experience working with legal, compliance or other regulated and complex industries or the ability to learn a complex domain exceptionally fast.<br />● Strong programme and project management skills; you keep multi-workstream initiatives moving and your clients confident.<br />● Excellent communication skills — written, verbal and interpersonal. You can lead boardroom conversations with legal and professional services leaders and roll up your sleeves with hands-on teams.<br />● High EQ: you know when to listen, when to advise and when to act.<br />● A love of fast-paced, early-stage environments where you help build the playbook, not just follow it.<br />● Fluency with metrics and driven by data, customer health and outcomes over process.<br />● Willingness to travel internationally around 25% of the time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Legora is an Equal Opportunity Employer</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Legora, we believe great teams are built on diversity of thought and experience. We’re proud to be an equal opportunity employer and committed to creating an inclusive, high-performance culture where everyone can do their best work. We welcome people of all backgrounds and don’t discriminate based on race, color, religion, national origin, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by law.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/legora/senior-engagement-manager-london-435445","tags":["Engagement"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792399214},{"slug":"programme-manager-trade-moorgate-323347","company_name":"Checkatrade","title":"Programme Manager (Trade)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Powering Great Work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We started as the place to find a trusted trade. Now, as we shape the future of home improvement, we're building the tech to transform that landscape for everyone - better products, smarter data, AI where it actually helps - so trades can spend less time on admin and consumers can find someone they trust, first time. That's Powering Great Work, and it's why every team here exists:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🔧 Trades spend less time on admin and more on winning work and growing their business</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🏠 Homeowners get a trusted trade, first time, every time</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚀 We get to build products that change homes and lives across the country</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Programme Manager (Trade) in Retention, you'll turn strategy into delivery that actually sticks. You won't manage the teams, but you'll shape how they work, what they work on, and whether the initiatives our Head of Operations is driving make it into everyday practice. You'll sit across the whole of Trade Lifecycle, working with Finance, Product, Engineering, Sales and CRM so the right things get built, rolled out and embedded, not just kicked off.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The job, unfiltered:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the delivery of Trade Lifecycle's most critical initiatives end to end, from scoping and planning through to execution and review.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead tooling and systems changes across Retention, Credit Control and Trade Support: define requirements, manage timelines and make sure the teams can use the new systems well.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Spot where processes are inconsistent, undocumented or breaking under scale, and fix them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the change management side: stakeholder communication, rollout sequencing, training and adoption tracking, so new ideas don't fade after launch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the senior point of coordination between Trade Lifecycle and Finance, Product, Engineering, Sales and CRM.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and maintain the reporting that shows whether strategic initiatives are working, and own the KPI framework for transformation delivery.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The fit:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depth of experience in a programme, operations or strategy delivery role, ideally in a high-growth tech or marketplace business.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A track record of delivering complex, cross-functional initiatives from design to measurable outcome. Not just managing the plan, but owning the result.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong project management instincts: you hold several workstreams at once, spot dependencies before they become blockers and keep senior stakeholders informed without overwhelming them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading tooling or systems rollouts in an operational environment, and you understand the change management challenge as well as the technical one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence with project management tools (Jira, Asana, Monday or similar) and reporting tools (Tableau, Looker, or advanced Sheets/Excel).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>(Don't self-select out because you don't tick every box. We'd rather meet you.)</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you get</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">💰 Competitive salary, annual bonus &amp; equity scheme</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🩺 Health, wellbeing and learning support</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🚲 Gym membership, Smart Tech Scheme, Cycle Scheme</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">🎂 Birthday/special day leave, buy &amp; sell holiday scheme</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">❤️ 1 week's paid charity leave, and more</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How this goes</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Screening call with one of our Talent Acquisition Partners</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First stage: interview with Head of Operations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Second stage interview with our Operations Manager </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Final stage: panel interview including case study </p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Not this one? Stay close anyway. Join the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/checkatrade/form/register-interest"><u>Talent Community</u></a> and we'll ping you the second something better fits.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About us<br /><br /></strong>We’re Checkatrade – the UK’s leading platform for finding a tradesperson. With more than 50,000 trades listed and over 6 million reviews, we help homeowners get jobs done right and help tradespeople grow their business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re growing fast, with big plans to become the go-to brand for home improvements. If you care about great work, take pride in the details, and want to make an impact, you’ll fit right in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/checkatrade/programme-manager-trade-moorgate-323347","tags":["Commercial  & Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Moorgate London","created_at":1792399214},{"slug":"head-of-enablement-united-kingdom-222613","company_name":"Aveni","title":"Head of Enablement","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Head of Enablement</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Do you love building something from scratch, and turning busy professionals into confident users of cutting-edge technology?</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for a <strong>Head of Enablement</strong> to build and lead the function that educates thousands of users on <strong>Aveni Assist</strong> and <strong>Aveni Detect</strong>. Our clients buy Aveni for their advice and compliance teams and your job is to win them over with programmes that are engaging, scalable, and genuinely useful.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About Aveni</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aveni is an award-winning technology company. We use advanced AI to enable scalable efficiency for financial services companies, combining world-leading Natural Language Processing (NLP) and Large Language Model (LLM) expertise with deep financial services domain experience to drive enterprise-wide productivity. We’re using the latest in AI to automate and innovate, empowering businesses to achieve exceptional productivity and compliance outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>About the Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a build role. Our user base has grown to thousands of users on Assist alone, and a single client can have 2,500 users to train. You’ll design how enablement works at Aveni - the processes, standards, tooling, and team structure - and maybe even launch an Aveni Certification across different user types.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Core Focus Allocation</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>60% Framework &amp; Process:</strong> Process design, programme architecture, and training automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>20% Team Leadership:</strong> Hiring, coaching, and scaling your enablement team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>20% Hands-On Delivery:</strong> High-impact in-person and online training execution if we hit capacity</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What You’ll Be Doing</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enablement Strategy:</strong> Own enablement for <em>Assist</em> and <em>Detect</em>, defining what great looks like for each user type and customer segment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Aveni Certification:</strong> Design and launch programmes featuring LMS courses, quizzes, and digital badges aligned to our delivery model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Scalable Programmes:</strong> Build onboarding, new-joiner, refresher, and feature-launch training that reaches thousands of users with minimal manual effort.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Blended Delivery:</strong> Run in-person and online training, delivering critical sessions yourself where it matters most or where we have hit capacity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Operating Model:</strong> Set the operational processes, scheduling rhythm, and quality expectations for the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Measurement &amp; Analytics:</strong> Track engagement, completion, adoption, and competency, using data to continuously improve outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Team Leadership:</strong> Hire, coach, and grow a high-performing team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-Functional Partnership:</strong> Work closely with Customer Success, Implementation, Product, and Sales.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Function Builder:</strong> Proven experience building an enablement, training, or customer education function and establishing its operational model.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Training Manager Background:</strong> Strong hands-on experience delivering training both in person and online.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Enterprise Certification Design:</strong> Experience designing programmes or certifications in an LMS for thousands of end users.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>B2B2C / Large-Scale Adoption:</strong> Experience enabling the end users of enterprise client organisations at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Adoption Journeys:</strong> Proven track record running customer-facing onboarding and adoption journeys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Key Attributes:</strong> Quick-thinking, emotionally intelligent, customer-obsessed, and process-driven.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Nice to Have</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with both high-touch and self-serve enablement models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Financial services, wealth management, or regulated industry experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Background in automating customer training journeys.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scale-up or start-up experience.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Benefits</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Environment &amp; Culture:</strong> Collaborative, innovative work environment with substantial career growth opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time Off:</strong> 34 days holiday plus your birthday off (inclusive of bank holidays).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equity:</strong> Share options—we believe in shared success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Professional Growth:</strong> Skills development and continuous learning support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work Flexibility:</strong> Fully remote and flexible working options (remote, co-working spaces, or hybrid).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health &amp; Protection:</strong> Life insurance, income protection, and private healthcare.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wellbeing:</strong> 24/7 Employee Assistance Programme (EAP) for emotional wellbeing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks &amp; Savings:</strong> Cycle to Work scheme, pension match up to 5%, and exclusive retailer discounts.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Join Us in Making a Difference</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Aveni, we believe that diversity drives innovation. We’re committed to building a team that reflects the diverse communities we serve and creating an inclusive workplace where everyone feels valued and empowered to contribute their best work. We know that some people only apply when they meet 100% of the requirements, but we’d like to hear from you anyway.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Apply now to join us on our mission to transform the financial services industry through AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/aveni/head-of-enablement-united-kingdom-222613","tags":["Customer"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"United Kingdom","created_at":1792399213},{"slug":"director-of-engineering-london-180335","company_name":"True Talent Solutions Partners","title":"Director of Engineering","description":"<h3>About the Role</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">A Series A AI risk management company is hiring a Director of Engineering to lead and scale its engineering organization. You will shape the leadership structure, operating practices, and technical culture across AI engineering and deployment engineering.</p><h3>What You'll Do</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scale the engineering organization from an early-stage team to 100 or more people while maintaining strong execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire and develop engineering leaders, and establish structures for effective collaboration across a globally distributed team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set planning rhythms, prioritization frameworks, hiring standards, onboarding practices, and performance expectations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Represent engineering capabilities in discussions with customers, partners, and the broader technical community.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with company leadership on organizational strategy, headcount planning, and product and go-to-market decisions.</p></li></ul><h3>What We're Looking For</h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 5 years of engineering leadership experience, including direct accountability for hiring, team structure, and leadership development while scaling an organization from approximately 25 to 100 or more people.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience leading globally distributed teams and coordinating across regions in a startup or high-growth environment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical judgment across AI engineering and deployment or production infrastructure, including experience spanning AI research, applied machine learning, and production deployment.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience at a fast-growing company beyond Series B and familiarity with the organizational challenges of scaling.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong public-facing technical communication skills and a degree from a highly regarded institution or equivalent professional experience.</p></li></ul><h3>Compensation &amp; Benefits</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Base salary: $325,000 to $365,000 USD annually. Visa sponsorship is not available.</p><h3>Location</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid in London, United Kingdom, with in-person work four days per week and one remote day on Tuesday or Friday.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/true-talent-solutions-partners/director-of-engineering-london-180335","tags":["Client Roles"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1792388415},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-london-142611","company_name":"Faculty","title":"Senior Software Engineer","description":"<h2><strong>Why Faculty? </strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />We established Faculty in 2014 because we thought that AI would be the most important technology of our time. Since then, we’ve worked with over 350 global customers to transform their performance through human-centric AI. You can read about our real-world impact <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://faculty.ai/impact">here</a>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We don’t chase hype cycles. We innovate, build and deploy responsible AI which moves the needle - and we know a thing or two about doing it well. We bring an unparalleled depth of technical, product and delivery expertise to our clients who span government, finance, retail, energy, life sciences and defence.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our business, and reputation, is growing fast and we’re always on the lookout for individuals who share our intellectual curiosity and desire to build a positive legacy through technology.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is an epoch-defining technology, join a company where you’ll be empowered to envision its most powerful applications, and to make them happen.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the Team</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bringing medicine to patients is complex, expensive and high-risk. Faculty’s Life Science’s team is concentrated on building AI solutions which optimise the research and commercialisation of life-changing therapies.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We partner with major pharma firms, academic research centres and MedTech start-ups to design and deliver solutions which address critical healthcare challenges, and help to democratise health for all.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>About the role:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Senior Software Engineer, we’ll look to you to lead development and deployment of cutting-edge AI and software systems for our diverse clients. You’ll design, build, and deploy scalable, production-grade ML/software and infrastructure that meets rigorous operational and ethical standards.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an ambitious, cross-functional role requiring a blend of technical expertise and confident client-facing skills.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leading technical scoping and architectural decisions for high-impact ML and software systems</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Designing and building production-grade ML/software, tools, and scalable infrastructure</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Defining and implementing best practices and standards for deploying machine learning at scale across the business</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborating with engineers, data scientists, product managers, and commercial teams to solve critical client challenges and leverage opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Acting as a trusted technical advisor to customers and partners, translati