ight:1.5em">Analyse Fin’s performance across markets, languages, use cases, and rollout phases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor handovers to human agents and customer satisfaction signals.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track corrective actions, owners, and validation status.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve the documentation and versioning of Fin’s evaluation framework.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Share clear, actionable feedback with product, engineering, content, and data teams.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>YOU ARE IN THE RIGHT PLACE IF: ⭐</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are completing a Master 2 degree in Data Science, Applied Mathematics, Statistics, or another engineering discipline.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong analytical and problem-solving skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are comfortable working with data and investigating anomalies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are interested in generative AI, machine learning, or LLM evaluation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can structure and communicate findings clearly in English.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are curious, detail-oriented, pragmatic, and comfortable investigating ambiguous problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can distinguish facts, hypotheses, and open questions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">BONUS POINT : Experience with LLM evaluation, prompt evaluation, conversational AI, or human-in-the-loop systems is a plus. French is helpful but not required.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>ABOUT THE INTERNSHIP:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start date: January 2027</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Duration : 6 months</p></li><li><p style="min-hei