ios.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">RF Measurement: Run hands-on characterization with network and spectrum analyzers, and simulate new antenna iterations with EM software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Electromagnetic Compatibility: Lead EMC troubleshooting and pre-compliance testing, identifying and removing blockers early.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PCB Collaboration: Work with PCB designers to review routing, shielding and RF layout.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architecture Ownership: Review and own the RF architecture across product lines, including link budgets and system-level RF performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentoring: Act as the team's RF subject matter expert, coaching junior engineers on RF layout principles and EMC mitigation.<br /></p></li></ul><h2>Candidate Requirements</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Education: Bachelor's or Master's degree in Electrical Engineering, RF Engineering, Telecommunications or a related field.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience: Proven track record taking complex wireless devices from concept to mass production, including clearing strict EMC compliance hurdles. Background in aerospace, commercial drones or GNSS products is a strong advantage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">GNSS: Solid grounding in GNSS, including hands-on use of a GNSS test bench to simulate edge-case environments, and an understanding of effects such as multipath.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Antenna Design: Experience designing custom antennas under tight mechanical and space constraints, with EM simulation tools.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">RF &amp; EMC: Strong command of RF fundamentals and measurement equipment (network and spectrum analyzers); comfortable working in an anechoic chamber.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mindset: Analytical, meticulous, structured and resilient; a hands-on problem-solver who works autonomously and collaborates well.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communication &amp; Influence: Excellent written and verbal communication, capable of leading diverse principals, from junior members to senior executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commitment: 100% dedication to Harmattan AI's mission, vision, and ambitious growth plans, ready to go the extra mile to ensure operational excellence.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to hearing how you can help shape the future of autonomous defense systems at Harmattan AI.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/harmattan-ai/rf-engineer-gnss-lausanne-129720","tags":["R&D"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lausanne","created_at":1792442418},{"slug":"machine-learning-research-engineer-visual-navigation-lausanne-360098","company_name":"Harmattan Ai","title":"Machine Learning Research Engineer – Visual Navigation","description":"<h3><strong>About Us</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Harmattan AI is a next-generation defense prime building autonomous and scalable defense systems. Following the close of a $200M Series B, valuing the company at $1.4 billion, we are expanding our teams and capabilities to deliver mission-critical systems to allied forces.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our work is guided by clear values: building technologies with real-world impact, pursuing excellence in everything we do, setting ambitious goals, and taking on the hardest technical challenges. We operate in a demanding environment where rigor, ownership, and execution are expected.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As an ML Research Engineer in the <strong>Visual Navigation team</strong>, you will join us at an early stage to heavily influence our technical di